# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored.
# The DeepSeek API key is not an environment variable — it lives in the
# harness's SQLite settings table. Set it after the stack is up with
#   docker compose exec harness harness config set deepseek.api_key sk-...
# Key from https://platform.deepseek.com/api_keys — prepaid, needs balance.

# The models, run budgets, tool limits, worker sizes, and retention windows
# are not environment variables either — they are settings in the same table,
# changed with `harness config set` (or from the settings screen) without a
# rebuild. `harness config list` shows every setting, its default, and which
# ones need a restart. The environment below is bootstrap only: where the
# database lives, where the service binds, and the API base URL.

# Optional overrides. Defaults are in docs/MODELS.md.
# DEEPSEEK_BASE_URL=https://api.deepseek.com
# DEEPSEEK_THINKING=true

# Price table. Never compiled in — see docs/DESIGN.md §4.9.
# DEEPSEEK_PRICE_TABLE=configs/prices.json

# Clones the repositories a work request names, and authenticates the git
# and gh calls an agent session makes afterwards. Needed for private repos.
# The harness container writes it to a credential file at startup.
# GITHUB_TOKEN=github_pat_...

# Holds harness.db (SQLite, WAL) and the sessions/ disk mirror.
# DEEPSEEK_DATA_DIR=data
# Raw HTTP capture, on by default, under <DataDir>/http. Off ("0" or
# "false") installs no capture wrapper. The log grows without bound, so
# this is the switch an operator whose disk is filling turns off.
# DEEPSEEK_HTTP_LOG=true

# NATS. `docker compose up -d` starts JetStream on the ports below.
# NATS_URL=nats://127.0.0.1:4222
# Host port overrides for docker-compose.yml. Set these if another project on
# this machine already binds the NATS defaults.
# NATS_CLIENT_PORT=4222
# NATS_MONITOR_PORT=8222

# The directory each run's own workspace is created under, one folder per
# session id holding that run's clones. Unset means every request fails
# before its session starts — see docs/DESIGN.md §4.10. Under docker compose
# the harness service sets this to HARNESS_WORKSPACES below — the same path on
# both sides of the mount; this value is for running the binary on the host.
# DEEPSEEK_WORKSPACE_ROOT=/abs/path/to/workspaces

# The harness service in docker-compose.yml. It reads this file for the
# GitHub token and model settings (the DeepSeek API key lives in the
# database, set with `harness config set`), and overrides NATS_URL, the HTTP
# address, the data directory, and the workspace root with its own container
# paths.
# The workspace root, mounted at this same absolute path inside the container
# (docs/WORKTREES.md, "Path parity") — so it must be a path the host's docker
# daemon can resolve, and on Docker Desktop one it is allowed to share.
# Pinning it outside the repo keeps personal directory names out of every path
# a session prints. Absolute: the compose default is ${PWD}, the shell's
# directory rather than the project's.
# HARNESS_WORKSPACES=/Users/Shared/harness-workspaces
# Host port for the web UI and the /api/... API — the MCP launch server
# mounts at /mcp on this same port, published on loopback only.
# HARNESS_HTTP_PORT=8080

# The MCP launch server, served by `harness serve` at /mcp on the same HTTP
# port as the web UI. Loopback by default — see docs/DESIGN.md's MCP launch
# server section.
# readonly or full. permission_mode is required on every launch, so this is
# an operator's optional limit on top: set readonly to refuse full runs from
# this server, which then error rather than being quietly downgraded.
# DEEPSEEK_MCP_PERMISSION_CEILING=full
# Model the "flash" profile launches.
# DEEPSEEK_MCP_FLASH_MODEL=deepseek-v4-flash
# How long deepseek_agent waits for an `accepted` message before reporting
# the request as queued instead of running.
# DEEPSEEK_MCP_ACCEPTED_WAIT_MS=3000
# The harness's read-only HTTP API, for the resources this server proxies.
# Defaults to the address `harness serve` derives from its own bind address;
# this value is for running the binary directly on the host with the API on
# a different origin.
# DEEPSEEK_HARNESS_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080
# Base URL used to build transcript links handed back to a caller so a human
# can watch a run. Defaults to DEEPSEEK_HARNESS_BASE_URL, which is wrong
# under docker compose (a browser cannot resolve the harness service's
# internal name) — the harness service sets this explicitly there.
# DEEPSEEK_HARNESS_PUBLIC_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080
# The http.external_url setting (settings page, `harness config set`, or
# PUT /api/settings) takes precedence over DEEPSEEK_HARNESS_PUBLIC_URL when
# set, and is the preferred way to change this without a redeploy.

# docker-compose.prod.yml reads .env.prod instead of this file, and writes its
# ports and paths out rather than reading them from either. Copy the
# environment overrides above into .env.prod by hand when a change is meant to
# reach production; the settings-table values (limits, models, API keys) are
# set inside each environment with `harness config set` and do not come from
# either file. See the README's "A production stack beside the dev one".

# The test broker in docker-compose.test.yml, started by scripts/test.sh.
# The integration tests use this and ignore NATS_URL, which names the
# deployment's broker. Override both together, or the suite and the broker
# it starts disagree on the port.
# HARNESS_TEST_NATS_PORT=4422
# HARNESS_TEST_NATS_URL=nats://127.0.0.1:4422
